pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: `L1 L2 ==> C` pushed a big-M term whose coefficient is C's
% normalized degree. For a negative degree -- exactly when C is trivially true,
% so the reification is a tautology -- `normalize()` flipped each pushed term to
% `|degree| * Lj` and raised the degree to `(k-1) * |degree|`. With two premise
% literals `x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 >= -1` was stored as the clause `1 x1 1 x2 1 x3 >= 1`,
% which this `e` used to match. It must now parse to the tautology `1 x1 >= -1`.
f 1 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 >= -1 : 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
